This is the one task you will do every morning.

## Where it is

**My Class → Students** in the side drawer.

The attendance column on that roster **only appears for teacher accounts**. If you are looking at
the same class as an admin, or through **Students → Classes** rather than **My Class**, the column
is not there — that is why an administrator cannot see what you are describing.

## Marking a student present

1. Open **My Class → Students**.
2. Find the student in the roster.
3. Select the attendance control on their row. It marks them immediately — there is no separate save
   step, and no confirmation.

Work down the list. The control shows each student's current state, so a glance down the column
tells you who is still unmarked.

## Unmarking

Selecting the control again on an already-marked student asks **Are you sure you want to unmark
attendance?** and, on confirming, removes the record. Use this for a genuine mistake, not for
marking someone absent — see below.

## Present, absent and unmarked

There are only two states stored: a student **has** an attendance record for today, or they do not.

- **Marked** = present.
- **Unmarked** = not recorded present. That covers absent, late-and-not-yet-arrived, and
  you-haven't-got-to-them-yet, and the reports cannot tell those apart.

So the register is only meaningful once you have been through the whole class. Finish the list.

## Cards and scans

Where students carry RFID cards, scanning at the gate creates the same record you would create by
hand — a student who has already scanned in will show as marked before you start. You are topping up
the ones the gate missed, not duplicating it.

A student with no card number on their record can never be marked by scanning, only by you. If
someone is permanently missing from the scans, their record probably has no RFID — see
[Add a Student](/docs/educonnect-tutorial-add-a-student).

## If a student is missing from the roster

They are enrolled in a different class, or not enrolled at all. Adding them is an office task, not a
teacher one — ask for them to be added to your class rather than creating a duplicate record.

